= Conclusion

The integrated pipeline reaches mean mask IoU $0.921$ and mean boundary $F_1$ $0.433$ across a $55$-frame hand-labeled subset spanning eleven distinct VARTM infusion runs, against two reimplemented prior classical-CV pipelines that lack the peak-brightness reference, the darken-only delta, the dynamic-lag reference, the temporal lock, and the run-time camera-shift registration that the integrated configuration combines. A per-sample component-removal ablation on the same subset reports the marginal IoU effect of disabling each named primitive in turn; the marginal effects vary by sample, and the per-sample breakdown rather than the eleven-sample mean is the load-bearing piece. From that breakdown, a regime-indexed configuration lookup translates the per-sample evidence into preprocessing settings indexed by the run circumstances a practitioner can read off their own bench. The pipeline runs at $30$ frames per second on a single CPU. The empirical contribution of this paper is the integrated pipeline as a named composition, the per-sample evidence that says which components are doing the work on which infusion regimes, and the lookup that translates that evidence into preprocessing settings for the next infusion that lands on the bench.
